s-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5255e65216fdefc285f9026a169e28ffaa9155ea2fa6611482a990103ec144</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary's reckoning with Orban's corrupt system picks up speed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f75c02dff29f77d46c735a1173d76fc3b3349947b3761e20c41addf33afc281</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:54:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714--fef6c98dbd47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar vowed to dismantle Orban's corrupt networks. High-profile figures are being arrested and many Hungarians are pushing for swift accountability, but the rule of law takes time.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham seeks 'hope again' at Labour Party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:497a341b40c058693f846f989248513b7d129b198bb763cd31a95d3b23d77ca6</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376--71e603fc9e60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham is seeking a delicate balance between optimism and realism at Labour's annual party conference. He promised hope and an end to "politics as usual" but also an "honest conversation" about difficult dilemmas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: As corruption cases multiply, experts question whether the anti-corruption drive is addressing the causes or just the symptoms.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26d9de5b08c567789b92574630fa5286610b9d0209cd807aea9d9e9195ffdf6e</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressin/a-79473031--8c7e71b0b3b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressing-the-causes-or-just-the-symptoms/a-79473031?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From a former president to the ex-intelligence chief, Albania is prosecuting senior officials at a rate once thought impossible. But do more prosecutions mean less corruption or simply better enforcement?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: US government questions bail for Fairford base suspects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d119cd2ded7ecfd154cbdb4d1b654fa996149fdfeb10522ede6febafc523d89</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803--3794b4b54f63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US government sees "the hand of a foreign actor" in the security scare at RAF Fairford, a hub for US heavy bombers in Europe. Donald Trump criticized the suspects being released on bail amid ongoing investigations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sicily: Mount Etna ash disrupts Catania flights again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbeba3fae2043ff7238239783059373698ed19776890946387fc928ef65f1abf</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sicily-mount-etna-ash-disrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773--6d2664a469ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sicily-mount-etna-ash-disrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A thick ash cloud from Mount Etna has been disrupting flights to Catania in Sicily for several days. Italy and Europe's most active volcano, Etna has impacted air travel several times this summer.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Comedian convicted for 'insulting' Erdogan in show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af597dda521778d1f7871a21217347e3a46cf0a72b053d40a4179adfded518bc</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759--b32d8c83cb81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Deniz Goktas was convicted of two of three charges, including "insulting" the president, but was released pending the appeal process. Nominally, Turkey is a secular country with free speech.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European cities seek ways of boosting affordable housing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af9ba64644a13c467fa362675f225b6cb3fd848c7f900d687a5c804d2dbbf860</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939--fc67dbf8271c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In many major urban centers of Europe, the housing shortage has become an explosive social issue. DW looks into various models that have been put in place across the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash over data centers tests Europe's AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27d5e3c7b08ddaa65e27607db6e5a8742cdd6ef3c259b061f8d35ad6c0df9c12</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800--224361aa983d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive data centers needed to run AI are triggering protests across Europe. Their operators counter that they boost digital sovereignty and energy independence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia expected to intensify hybrid war on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f125dd43f1dab4c00021343bcd36bddd09e0aafda0a988d12a32071cff1f0cb</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596--b27c55cf76ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone explosions, airspace violations, arson attacks: Poland, Romania, and Moldova are now regularly targeted in Russian attacks against Ukraine. More governments are calling these attacks deliberate acts of aggression.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russian classroom propaganda glorifies dying for your country, students say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08b6597d003880a7d8d535af2793b898a7b23dc291fce8b58187ab3d9bbf3a96</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-classroom-propaganda-promotes-dying-for-country-students-say/a-79417294--0c26f56386a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-classroom-propaganda-glorifies-dying-for-your-country-students-say/a-79417294?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Russian government has stepped up its efforts to spread patriotic propaganda in schools. DW spoke to students about textbooks that portray the West as hostile and promote sacrifice for the nation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'Lithuanian skies are NATO skies': DW speaks with Lithuanian premier Mindaugas Sinkevicius</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4571689c679a9a4273f517b26505e17d634f3f66cf45a2183f54545af063149d</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lithuanian-skies-are-nato-skies-dw-speaks-with-lithuanian-premier-mindaugas-sinkevicius/a-79432394--2e48449cf03c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lithuanian-skies-are-nato-skies-dw-speaks-with-lithuanian-premier-mindaugas-sinkevicius/a-79432394?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a DW interview, Prime Minister Mindaugas Sinkevicius discussed threats to Lithuania from Russia and Belarus, NATO's need for stronger air defense and why military spending alone cannot ensure security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Bulgaria become a global leader in battery storage and what this means for the country's grid and energy market?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:879b05514359ec8ced3c250e6e4412e9f9964aace1ee2de918bf5e32e52e7ab3</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-bulgaria-become-a-global-leader-in-battery-storage-and-what-this-means-for-the-country-s-grid-an/a-79428289--917b8ba9c523.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-bulgaria-become-a-global-leader-in-battery-storage-and-what-this-means-for-the-country-s-grid-and-energy-market/a-79428289?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In under two years, Bulgaria has become one of the world's most battery-intensive energy markets. Can the surge last — and what will it mean for conventional power generators?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy to ban burqa in schools, limit foreign pupils</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0d41a97f62f19168ec6c7a4e59d95fd44537a77379ed5b3ebdaeec0457c3c41</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-to-ban-burqa-in-schools-limit-foreign-pupils/a-79423432--d459be98ca4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-to-ban-burqa-in-schools-limit-foreign-pupils/a-79423432?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni’s government has passed new school rules capping the number of students who don't speak fluent Italian and banning face coverings.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czech PM Andrej Babis reiterates importance of NATO for his country but rejects calls to increase defense spending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69ef430646ff8a2abfdf63a5e5767adb124cd213860b781c6ebe7e7d93f496d3</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czech-pm-andrej-babis-reiterates-importance-of-nato-for-his-country-but-rejects-calls-to-increase-de/a-79411066--415ccd460a40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czech-pm-andrej-babis-reiterates-importance-of-nato-for-his-country-but-rejects-calls-to-increase-defense-spending/a-79411066?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US and NATO want Czechia to spend more on defense. Czech Prime Minister Andrej Babis says Prague cannot afford faster increases, despite growing warnings about the threat from Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'Pope fever' takes hold as Pope Leo visits France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c6b114aa1be7d8e63979e66049d23a2db47c38ab4d0fa099785fb29dd6eb737</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-fever-takes-hold-as-pope-leo-visits-france/a-79401291--1edb64ca4ad9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-fever-takes-hold-as-pope-leo-visits-france/a-79401291?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV is expected to draw huge crowds during his visit to France. As part of his trip, he's also set to address Europe's future and some of the challenges ahead.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Slovakia: PM Robert Fico's NATO Article 5 remarks spark criticism and raise questions about his country's NATO commitment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8869ad39c92ba50a15817003c44696ea08fdde1007b4e8bfa87f2c9b578e2c7</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-count/a-79387050--e3e0d18cd9d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-country-s-nato-commitment/a-79387050?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico says he fears war and will do everything he can to keep his country out of one. Critics say his remarks risk weakening NATO, the alliance that was designed to prevent such a war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Famine threatens the Ukrainian town of Oleshky in the southern Kherson region as Russia delays creating a humanitarian evacuation corridor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c06920aacda7130c40632bae2d6ec0c1c3149fcea3046dc36450d06bd2e5fb93</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/famine-threatens-the-ukrainian-town-of-oleshky-in-the-southern-kherson-region-as-russia-delays-creat/a-79380887--1d1c80d27c3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/famine-threatens-the-ukrainian-town-of-oleshky-in-the-southern-kherson-region-as-russia-delays-creating-a-humanitarian-evacuation-corridor/a-79380887?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Food supplies to the town of Oleshky, in the occupied part of the southern Kherson region, have been cut off since May. Efforts by Kyiv to negotiate the evacuation of civilians with Moscow have been largely unsuccessful.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
